---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/i18n.js';

const lang = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title={t('gehealthcare.meta.title', lang)}
  description={t('gehealthcare.meta.description', lang)}
  ogUrl="https://kajoble.com/en/gehealthcare"
>
  <div id="main" class="alt">
    <section id="one">
      <div class="inner">
        <header class="major">
          <h1>{t('gehealthcare.title', lang)}</h1>
        </header>
        <span class="image main"><img src="/images/geheath.jpg" alt="GE Healthcare" /></span>
        <p>From the outset, I took a leadership role in the Common User Interface project, improving the quality of synthesizer and distributor reports by introducing more detailed, higher-quality graphical representations. I modernized the user interface by migrating from WinForms to a WPF vector architecture, significantly improving usability and maintainability. In parallel, I led the development of the electro-mechanical rotary actuator control at the PLC level and improved the radioactivity detector calibration process by replacing manual operations with algorithm-driven automation.</p>
        <p><span class="image left"><img src="/images/fastlab.jpg" alt="" /></span>Beyond user interfaces, my work focused on building robust, reliable systems within a highly regulated medical environment. I designed calibration workflows, anomaly tracking mechanisms, and custom event logging to ensure traceability and compliance with validation and verification standards. I was deeply involved in system documentation, UML modeling, and GaMP-compliant validation processes, ensuring that software quality met both technical and regulatory expectations.</p>
        <br/><br/>
        <p><span class="image right"><img src="/images/fastlab-software.jpg" alt="" /></span>I also contributed to the long-term evolution of the platform by leading major migrations, integrating third-party components, managing database tooling, and supporting IT operations. This experience laid the foundation of my career: delivering mission-critical software where precision, safety, and reliability are non-negotiable.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="two">
      <div class="inner">
        <header class="major">
          <h2>{t('gehealthcare.techStack', lang)}</h2>
        </header>
        <p>C#, .NET Framework, .NET Core, ASP.NET Core, Blazor (Server & WebAssembly), WCF, WCF RIA Services, Entity Framework, Entity Framework Core, Minimal APIs</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
